    "topic": "openlifescienceai/medmcqa",
    "problem": "Q: Consider the following problem. The sensation of creeping bugs over the body is a feature of which of the following poison? A) Cocaine B) Diazepam C) Barbiturates D) Brown sugar",
    "solution": "A: Answer: A) Cocaine Explanation: Magnan's symptom or cocaine bugs is a characteristic feature of cocaine poisoning. In this patient's feels as if grains of sand are lying under the skin or small insects (cocaine bugs) are creeping on the skin (formication) giving rise to itching sensation, with resultant excoriation leading to irregular scratches and ulcers. Ref: Essentials of Forensic\u2026",
